{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/465803-a-couple-of-questions-about-demon","id":465803,"title":"A couple of questions about Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-02T02:15:48-07:00","id":465803,"title":"A couple of questions about Demon","content":"Hello, first time post in the Demon forum, just got acquainted with Demon, and I like it a lot, especially the use of the second edition rules, but I get a few questions now:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. A Demon at Primum 10, has 100 of Aether; unlike the other supernatural races in second edition (Vampire, Werewolf), who get 75 of their &quot;fuel stat&quot;; is this a leftover of first edition or Demons are meant to have higher &quot;fuel stat&quot; capacity than other supernaturals?<br /> <br /> 2. At character creation Demons can buy 1 dot Primum per 3 Merit dots, unlike Vampires or Werewolves who pay 5 Merit dots per dot of Power stat, is this a leftover of first edition or intentional?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your answers and time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T02:28:57-07:00","id":465826,"title":"","content":"Welcome to Demon!<br /> <br /> 1. Yup, 100 Aether. Might be because a hundred is a round number that's easy to remember, and demons are more likely than other templates (except mummies) to temporarily jump up to ten dots of their &quot;power stat,&quot; due to their ability to go loud. Also note that Aether is, in my experience, relatively precious for WoD &quot;fuel points;&quot; most means of refueling are a big deal unto themselves, and those that aren't either put your Cover at risk to use too much (entering demonic form) or pretty slow to harvest (Suborned Infrastructure).<br /> <br /> 2. This is a leftover; the final version of the book raises the cost to five Merit dots per starting dot of Primum, in line with the rest of second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:38:10-07:00","id":467375,"title":"","content":"Both are likely leftovers. Remember, Demon was designed and was released before Blood and Smoke, but after the God Machine Chronicles. The Lashing Out/Nimbus/Aspects that wolves, mages, vamps all have is notably missing, for instance. <br /> <br /> There's a lot of little things in Demon that don't perfectly match up with how post-B&amp;S supernaturals do it. That said, in a pure-Demon game, it doesn't matter. In a crossover game (where everyone is a different supernatural), its actually not that noticeable. Lets face it, even when Going Loud, when do you use over 75 plasm without being swarmed by angels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:15:34-07:00","id":467554,"title":"","content":"One major thing with Werewolves and Vampires, at least, is that they are predators. Being Alphas and detecting other Alpha Predators is an aspect of the game. Demons are more about being hidden. Being hidden, not knowing if someone is a Demon or Angel or neither, is part of the game. I don't think the lashing out sort of stuff is bad at all, but different games have different themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T04:31:44-07:00","id":468290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/465803-a-couple-of-questions-about-demon?p=467554#post467554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One major thing with Werewolves and Vampires, at least, is that they are predators. Being Alphas and detecting other Alpha Predators is an aspect of the game. Demons are more about being hidden. Being hidden, not knowing if someone is a Demon or Angel or neither, is part of the game. I don't think the lashing out sort of stuff is bad at all, but different games have different themes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would agree if we were just talking about predator auras, Baron. I read the post by Rose too; however, we're not talking about Auras, which puts this into an entirely different ballpark.<br /> <br /> From the sounds of it, Prometheans and Mages will have their own Lashing Out equivalents as well. Mage will be using theirs as part of their Nimbus, and clearly, they are not a form of predators. So, predator auras and lashing out equivalents are really comparing apples and oranges. While they may be connected in Vampire, they really have two different purposes from a game stand point. The point of auras are to detect another supernatural. Yes, that's something we might want to avoid (given spoofing, maybe maybe not, but that's a different discussion.). The point of Lashing Out is basically a supernatural &quot;mine is bigger than yours&quot; competition.<br /> <br /> As well, its completely in theme for a Demon to break Cover for a boost of power. Hells. That's the entire reason Exploits and partial/full transformations call for compromise checks, as well as allowing the use of Premum as a supernatural tolerance stat when in Cover.<br /> <br /> Thematically, having an Lashing Out equivalent isn't that different than using a partial transformation to get Glory and Terror or Corruption Aura and inflicting that; its just different mechanics to get there. So, you really can't say its not appropriate when all the appropriate parts are already built into the game.<br /> <br /> I truthfully suspect that, if Blood and Smoke hand come out before Demon was being written, DtD would have had a Lashing Out equivalent.<br /> <br /> <br /> All this is immaterial, really, since my point about the demon core remains. It has a lot of little things more in common with pre-2e than post-2e. Even the layout has more in common with the first edition books than the second edition books. Flowers of Hell immediately has taken more of a layout common to other 2e books, but the demon core is basically 1e layout. It should be as no surprise that a handful of mechanics aren't in line with 2e either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-04-2015, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T18:19:12-07:00","id":469714,"title":"","content":"Actually, it's intentional that there's no equivalent for lashing out for demons. Most of the rules/powers places that demons and vampires (the first two monsters designed for 2e) are different are on purpose.<br /> <br /> The 75/100 thing is an accident, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T01:40:54-07:00","id":469958,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the Demon equivalent to Lashing Out is going loud, after all that is what Lashing Out is about showing of your power and while Demons mainly try to keep of the radar when they do show of it is quite phenomenal.<br /> <br /> Sorry to hear that the 75/100 thing is an accident though as I liked the even number a lot better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T02:00:33-07:00","id":469983,"title":"","content":"Even talking about Lasing Out alone, I don't think it's not being there is a detriment. I don't have an issue with a game having it, and it certainly fits Vampire and Werewolf VERY well. I still don't think all games need it, or it being an oversight not to have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:25:28-07:00","id":473781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/465803-a-couple-of-questions-about-demon?p=469714#post469714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it's intentional that there's no equivalent for lashing out for demons. Most of the rules/powers places that demons and vampires (the first two monsters designed for 2e) are different are on purpose.<br /> <br /> The 75/100 thing is an accident, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just to summarize then:<br /> <br /> 1. It should be 75 Aether, not 100 Aether at Primum 10.<br /> <br /> 2. It should be 5 merit dots instead of 3 at character creation to increase Primum.<br /> <br /> Is it there any plans for an errata for Demon core?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}